ion of the storage of catecholamines"},{"label":"C","text":"Blockade of the amine reuptake pumps"},{"label":"D","text":"Nonselective MAO inhibition"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"General Pharmacology","answerAuditStatus":"newly_reasoned_provisional","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-b3117b93bb65","stem":"Characteristics of alfa-receptor antagonists include all of the following EXCEPT","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"General Pharmacology","topicOriginal":"General Pharmacology","subtopic":"Receptor","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"They cause a fall in peripheral resistance and blood pressure"},{"label":"B","text":"They cause epinephrine reversal (convert a pressor response to a depressor response)"},{"label":"C","text":"Bronchospasm"},{"label":"D","text":"They may cause postural hypotension and reflex tachycardia"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"General Pharmacology","answerAuditStatus":"newly_reasoned_provisional","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-bdb5809b2945","stem":"Which of the following drugs is an imidazoline derivative and a potent competitive antagonist at both alfa1 and alfa2 receptors?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"General Pharmacology","topicOriginal":"General Pharmacology","subtopic":"Receptor","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Prazosin"},{"label":"B","text":"Labetalol"},{"label":"C","text":"Phenoxybenzamine"},{"label":"D","text":"Phentolamine"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"